{#-
  The keepalive job (AC-6.4).  `rcac-keepalive setup-cron` used to build this
  header by hand in Python -- it was the only non-template site in the package
  that spelled the directive token, and what it spelled was the previous
  cluster's: a partition that does not exist on Gilbreth and a job-class
  annotation Gilbreth has no flag for.

  It renders from the same rcac_cli.gilbreth.SubmissionPlan as every other job,
  through the same shared header, so it inherits every AC-3 guarantee rather
  than a subset someone remembered to copy.  There is nothing keepalive-shaped
  in the header at all; the only local directives are -o/-e, whose filename
  pattern is per-template by design.

  `keepalive_script` is the path of the shell script this job runs.  The job
  itself is a `touch -a` sweep, which is why the caller pairs it with -q
  standby: uncharged, and the 4 hour cap is two orders of magnitude more than
  it needs.  C6 makes the login-node form the default (AC-6.5) precisely
  because even this job holds a GPU it never uses -- on Gilbreth every
  partition is a GPU partition and --gpus-per-node has a floor of 1.
-#}
#!/bin/bash
{% include '_sbatch_header.j2' %}
#SBATCH -o {{ scratch_root }}/logs/%x_%j.out
#SBATCH -e {{ scratch_root }}/logs/%x_%j.err

echo "$(date): keepalive job starting"
bash {{ keepalive_script }}
echo "$(date): keepalive job complete"
